# Terraform Native Test Standards — GCP

## Required Boilerplate
Every test file must include:
```hcl
mock_provider "google" {}

override_data {
  target = data.google_project.current
  values = {
    project_id = "test-project-123"
    number     = 123456789
    name       = "test-project"
  }
}
```

**Note:** This `override_data` block only works if the module under test defines `data "google_project" "current"` (typically in `main.tf`). If the module does not use that data source, omit the `override_data` block.

## All tests use `command = plan` — never `command = apply`.

## Required Variables
Include all `{{COMMON_VARS_FILE}}` variables in the `variables {}` block.
{{VARIABLE_GOTCHAS}}
<!-- Example: project_id must be a valid GCP project ID format (lowercase, max 30 chars) -->

## Standard Test Variables
```hcl
variables {
  prefix              = "test-auto"
  project_id          = "test-project-123"
  region              = "europe-west1"
  labels              = {}
  env_default_labels  = { managed_by = "terraform" }
}
```

## Organization
- One test file per feature area: `naming.tftest.hcl`, `labels.tftest.hcl`, etc.
- Run names: `snake_case` descriptive names
- Group related assertions in the same `run` block
